# UX-SPEC §3.13 · ADR 0023 — a Fleet that has never been run is set up by pointer: the first-run
# page's step 1 card opens New context, the name is typed, and the footer's Create makes it.
# With a context and no repository the page gives way to the Hub, which carries step 2: the
# Worktrees page leads with a primary Clone repo (header and body) and offers no New worktree,
# since there is nothing to branch from yet. Clone repo opens the Clone dialog, which the hermetic `empty` home cannot finish (it has no
# GitHub repositories to list), so its ✕ closes it. The title bar's context switcher then names
# the new context.
#
# Virtual-lane only: it takes shots.
fixture: empty
await idle 20000
assert key_contexts[0] == "FirstRun" && targets["first_run.step[0]"] exists

click first_run.step[0]
await dialog.name == Context 5000
assert dialog.fields[0].focused == true
type Pointer team
assert dialog.fields[0].value == "Pointer team"
click dialog.button[1]
await overlay absent 10000
await idle 10000
await screen == Hub 10000
assert key_contexts[0] != "FirstRun" && targets["worktrees.clone"] exists
assert targets["worktrees.empty.clone"] exists && targets["worktrees.new"] absent
shot context-created

click worktrees.empty.clone
await dialog.name == Clone 5000
await idle 10000
assert targets["dialog.button[1]"] exists
shot clone
click dialog.close
await overlay absent 5000

click titlebar.context
await targets["menu.item[0]"] exists 5000
shot context-menu
dump context-menu
quit
